# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_version_freshness.py" "EXTRACTOR VERSION FRESHNESS GATE: PASS" "graph-generation freshness (G3): freshness accounts for extractor/schema and exact-reference storage versions, not only commit SHA" "graph-generation freshness: graph_freshness compares stored/current extractor tokens and, when the new schema exposes it, stored/current semantic-reference versions. A same-SHA display-only v0 coordinate is behind v1 and cannot be path-locally patched; legacy schemas without the current token keep that axis inert. Behind feeds the existing full self-heal and failed-heal withheld-clear path." "a stored graph at CURRENT HEAD with a stale/null extractor stamp or semantic-reference generation is behind rather than a silent success; current generations stay fresh; old-schema keys remain inert; extractor self-heal behavior is proven end-to-end" 20
